course: dictionary
lesson: 12713
title: Dorm: a room full of beds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A dorm is a short, informal word for dormitory. It is a big bedroom with many beds, where lots of people sleep together. You will often find one at a boarding school or a camp.
explain: «Our dorm has eight beds, and everyone is already asleep.» Eight beds and a room full of sleeping people tell you a dorm is one big room, not a small bedroom for one person.
explain: In America, dorm can also mean a building at a college where students live. «Maya moved into her dorm at college in September.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? A place to live and sleep, with a room of her own or a shared room.
fact: Dorm is a short, informal word for dormitory.
fact: A dorm is a big room with many beds, often at a boarding school, camp or hostel.
fact: In the US, a dorm can be a building at a college where students live.
fact: Useful phrases are «dorm room» and «lights out in the dorm».
exercise: «The new pupils unpacked their bags in the dorm.» Where did the pupils unpack? | On the school bus | In the playground | In the kitchen | *In the dorm
exercise: Mia says, «Our dorm has eight beds.» What is a dorm? | A garden shed | A small bathroom with one sink | *A big bedroom with many beds | A type of bus
exercise: In America, Maya lives in a dorm at college. What is a dorm there? | A school library | A shop that sells books | *A building where students live | A park for sports
test:
Dorm is a short form of which longer word? | Dormant | *Dormitory | Doorway | Dormouse
Which phrase uses dorm correctly? | *Lights out in the dorm | Lights out in the sea | A dorm of fish swam past | The dorm was ringing a bell at the sea
exam:
Which sentence uses dorm correctly? | *«We slept in the dorm with twelve beds.» | «We ate the dorm for lunch.» | «The dorm kicked the football.» | «The dorm swam across the pond.»
